  {"id":"orc","name":"Orc","page":12,"source":"bestiary","roll20":[12,12],"movement":10,"category":"Nightkin","text":"Sun-shy nightkin long cast as villains by other peoples. The orcs themselves describe a history of being met with scorn and betrayed by supposed allies after promises of peace.","abilities":[{"id":"tough","name":"Tough","wp":3,"timing":"free","text":"At zero HP, activate to rally automatically — no WIL roll and no one needs to persuade you (core p.50)."}],"names":["Mauga","Muzorg","Radbag","Snagrat","Ug-Gash","Gor-Nakh"],"pcNotes":"Orc stat box lists Nocturnal (sunlight: bane on all rolls, D6 damage per stretch; avoided by thick cloud, dense foliage or full-cover clothing). The book does not say outright whether it applies to PCs; it is printed as a kin trait beside the Player Character note, so treat it as applying unless the GM rules otherwise.","traits":["Nocturnal (foliage)"]},
  {"id":"ogre","name":"Ogre","page":10,"source":"bestiary","roll20":[13,13],"movement":10,"category":"Nightkin","text":"Big, burly humanlike folk with moods that swing from gentle to violent — worst when drunk, hungover or nursing a toothache. Most live as brigands or mercenaries, often adopted into goblin clans (who like them) or orc clans (who look down on them).","abilities":[{"id":"body-slam","name":"Body Slam","wp":3,"timing":"action","text":"Unarmed melee attack with a boon dealing 2D6 bludgeoning plus damage bonus; it can't be parried. You may dash before it. Humanoids of Normal size or smaller who are hit are knocked down."}],"names":["Glorm","Barg","Arra","Klog","Orluk","Urla"],"pcNotes":"Ogres are Large creatures (core p.83: block 4×4 m, need a 1 m gap). Stat box also lists Nocturnal (bane on all rolls and D6 damage per stretch in direct sunlight; thick cloud, dense foliage or full-cover clothing prevents it). The book does not say explicitly whether these apply to PCs; both are listed as kin traits, so assume they do (GM call).","traits":["Nocturnal (foliage)","Large"],"size":"Large"},
  {"id":"goblin","name":"Goblin","page":6,"source":"bestiary","roll20":[14,14],"movement":10,"category":"Nightkin","text":"Small, hardy nightkin who often band together in clans and have served — and turned on — would-be conquerors. Known for scouting, ambushes and surviving on very little.","abilities":[{"id":"resilient","name":"Resilient","wp":1,"timing":"free","text":"Activate for a boon on a CON roll to resist poison or disease (core p.52–53), or to make camp without a Bushcraft roll (core p.103). Passive, no WP: you can always eat raw food without falling ill."}],"names":["Flifos","Ilola","Luts","Trulli","Luregg","Soli"],"pcNotes":"Stat box lists Nocturnal (direct sunlight: bane on all rolls, D6 damage per stretch; thick cloud, dense foliage or full-cover clothing avoids it). Not explicitly stated for PCs; listed as a kin trait, so assume it applies (GM call).","traits":["Nocturnal (foliage)"]},
  {"id":"hobgoblin","name":"Hobgoblin","page":8,"source":"bestiary","roll20":[15,15],"movement":10,"category":"Nightkin","text":"Tireless, loyal nightkin of forests and swamps who gather berries, fell timber, dig bog ore and hunt for sunken treasure at their clan leader's command — or raid settlements when that leader craves gold.","abilities":[{"id":"fearless","name":"Fearless","wp":2,"timing":"free","text":"Activate before rolling to automatically succeed on a WIL roll to resist fear (core p.52)."}],"names":["Gruush","Kloorg","Feeger","Aamash","Haggra","Ploot"],"pcNotes":"Stat box lists Nocturnal (direct sunlight: bane on all rolls, D6 damage per stretch; thick cloud or full-cover clothing avoids it — dense foliage is NOT listed for hobgoblins). Not explicitly stated for PCs; assume it applies (GM call).","traits":["Nocturnal"]},
  {"id":"frog-people","name":"Frog People","page":22,"source":"bestiary","roll20":[16,16],"movement":10,"category":"Rare Kin","text":"Reclusive wetland dwellers of uncertain origin — one tale blames a witch's curse on a fleeing prince and his consort. They fish and hunt the marshes, know them better than anyone, and talk to outsiders mostly through gestures (among themselves, blinks and croaks).","abilities":[{"id":"leaping","name":"Leaping","wp":3,"timing":"free","text":"Jump up to your Movement horizontally or half your Movement vertically with no Acrobatics roll. A melee attack made at the end of the jump gets a boon."}],"names":["Karkien","Boll","Papai","Tianen","Ribbiiti","Hotia"],"pcNotes":""},
  {"id":"karkion","name":"Karkion","page":26,"source":"bestiary","roll20":[17,17],"movement":10,"category":"Rare Kin","text":"Long-lived, bat-winged wanderers who travel alone gathering lore, above all about demons — the beings said to have destroyed their original world. They hope to keep this world from the same fate, but say little about themselves.","abilities":[{"id":"wings","name":"Wings","wp":1,"timing":"free","text":"Fly freely at the same speed as on foot; costs 1 WP per round of flight."}],"names":["Absu","Baatu","Gaar","Kibili","Maastu","Ubus"],"pcNotes":"Flight costs 1 WP per round and uses normal Movement (no separate fly speed). No other PC restrictions given.","flying":"wp"},
  {"id":"cat-people","name":"Cat People","page":16,"source":"bestiary","roll20":[18,18],"movement":10,"category":"Rare Kin","text":"Secretive, solitary folk thought to come from warmer southern lands. Kind but guarded individualists who cooperate only on their own terms, expert at going unnoticed and able to fight when pressed.","abilities":[{"id":"nine-lives","name":"Nine Lives","wp":"varies","wpNote":"Varies: 2 WP for a death roll; 1–3 WP for falls","timing":"free","text":"Spend 2 WP for a boon on a death roll (core p.50). Or, after the Acrobatics roll to reduce fall damage (core p.53), spend 1 WP per D6 to roll one fewer damage die, up to three."}],"names":["Star","Bast","Esme","Mira","Lune","Lapiz"],"pcNotes":""},
  {"id":"lizard-people","name":"Lizard People","page":28,"source":"bestiary","roll20":[19,19],"movement":10,"category":"Rare Kin","text":"Water-bound folk of bogs, swamps and river deltas with a hiss-and-click language outsiders easily garble. Most tribes fish eels, farm mussels and trade peacefully; a few warlike clans raid and take slaves under shaman kings who demand sacrifices.","abilities":[{"id":"camouflage","name":"Camouflage","wp":2,"timing":"free","text":"Activate for a boon on a Sneaking roll."}],"names":["[Cluck][hiss][hiss]","[Click][grr][shh][cluck]","[Hiss][click][click][hiss]","[Cluck][grr][hiss][hiss]","[Grr][grr]","[Hiss][shh][cluck][click][grr]"],"pcNotes":""},
  {"id":"satyr","name":"Satyr","page":36,"source":"bestiary","roll20":[20,20],"movement":10,"category":"Rare Kin","text":"Joy-worshipping forest folk who throw wild feasts of food, wine, song and dance in flowery glades, often with centaur and naiad friends. Any excuse will do for the next celebration.","abilities":[{"id":"raise-spirits","name":"Raise Spirits","wp":3,"timing":"action","text":"With song or verse, remove one chosen condition from someone who can hear you within 10 m. Can't target yourself."}],"names":["Aeson","Bartolome","Dianys","Priapos","Xander","Sebastian"],"pcNotes":"Stat box lists Melancholy: a satyr who can't celebrate with friends every day gets a bane on all rolls until it can party again. Not explicitly stated for PCs; listed as a kin trait, so assume it applies (GM call).","traits":["Melancholy"]}
