export const DB_KIN_LORE = [
  {"kin":"Goblin","page":6,"category":"Nightkin","text":"Clan-dwelling nightkin who once formed the core of the sorcerer Visimir's army against the Bloodfist orcs — until the scout Gutsy shot him for his treachery and led the surviving goblins into the forest.","encounter":"A dying woman stumbles up, begging the characters to follow the blood trail and save her beloved before he is eaten. A Spot Hidden or Hunting & Fishing roll follows the trail to a clearing where five merry goblins (two scouts, three warriors) are about to roast a bound man on a spit.","seed":"Goblin raiding bands from deep in a forest are robbing travelers of every station and growing bolder, sparing those who surrender but killing guards who resist. Behind them is the aging Gutsy, still bitter over Visimir's broken promise and spending the loot to arm a growing army that must be stopped before it threatens the whole region.","source":"bestiary"},
  {"kin":"Hobgoblin","page":8,"category":"Nightkin","text":"Hard-working, zealous nightkin who toil loyally for their clan leader in forests and swamps — though greedy lords may send them raiding.","encounter":"On a successful Spot Hidden roll a character spots boots poking out of a thicket: a slain adventurer clutching a bloody map with three landmarks. The circled ruin holds the survivors of clan Phubarra (a scout, a thief and three warriors) among many dead hobgoblins, mad with grief and thirsting for revenge.","seed":"A bog-ore mining village wants hobgoblins driven from the forest caves that now control the workings. The clan insists the land and mine were theirs first and the villagers stole them; old villagers may admit the truth if Persuaded, or neighboring settlements may know more. The characters must pick a side, broker peace, or walk away and let it come to blood.","source":"bestiary"},
  {"kin":"Ogre","page":10,"category":"Nightkin","text":"Massive, temperamental humanlike folk — mild one moment, belligerent the next, especially when drunk or in pain. Usually brigands or mercenaries, alone or within goblin or orc clans.","encounter":"At night the drunken, starving ogre Gvorm crashes into camp. Characters may attack at once, but an Awareness roll shows he only wants food; he rummages through packs and, if allowed to eat, turns friendly and helpful. Communicating with him at all takes a Persuasion roll.","seed":"Drunken ogres occupy a logging village, demanding all its beer and refusing to leave no matter how many barrels they get. Villagers beg the characters not to use force for fear the ogres will wreck everything; Persuasion might send them elsewhere (at a neighbor's expense), but the ogres soon tire of talk and start smashing the village.","source":"bestiary"},
  {"kin":"Orc","page":12,"category":"Nightkin","text":"Nightkin at constant war with other kin, who by their own telling have been met with arrogance and betrayed by every ally that promised them peace.","encounter":"The orc warrior Ogder hangs upside down from a snare, cursing and ordering the characters to cut him down. If they help, he grudgingly thanks them and warns of a giant spider nearby before heading back to his clan.","seed":"A badly wounded orc messenger collapses in the village square, gasping about a friend in a cave half a day west-northwest. Spot Hidden or Hunting & Fishing leads to a dead orc carrying Chieftain Grimner's letter warning that another orc clan will attack the village. Can the characters get back in time — and why did Grimner warn them? Only the feared chieftain can say.","source":"bestiary"},
  {"kin":"Cat People","page":16,"category":"Rare Kin","text":"Rare, solitary cat folk from the warm south who keep to the margins, cooperate only when it pays, and are masters of staying unseen.","encounter":"Excited wolf howls lead to a pack circling a tree where the cat man Amiz is fending them off with his sling. If the wolves are killed or driven off he climbs down, thanks the characters and goes his way — unless they Persuade him to join them.","seed":"The mage Haldur Grumble has lured the cat woman Inis to his tower and is magically interrogating her to learn about her kind, telling others he holds a demon so no one discovers he has unlawfully imprisoned a person. Her friend Feliz asks the characters to help break into the tower and free her.","source":"bestiary"},
  {"kin":"Frog People","page":22,"category":"Rare Kin","text":"Isolated marsh dwellers who live by fishing and hunting and know their wetlands better than anyone.","encounter":"A loud croak in a swamp heralds two young frog folk, Kaarvia and Saartia, flush from a good catch and eager to trade with the characters. Any hint of hostility and they bolt into the swamp.","seed":"The mage Ulvalf hires the characters to escort him to an ancient temple ruin now lost in a vast swamp, and is told to hire the frog woman Quaark as guide. First they must find her settlement; then she demands they kill a giant amoeba that has slain several of her friends before she will lead them to the ruin.","source":"bestiary"},
  {"kin":"Karkion","page":26,"category":"Rare Kin","text":"Lone, long-lived scholars from a world destroyed by demons, roaming to learn all they can — especially about demonic forces — so this world is spared.","encounter":"Deep in a forest the karkion mage Sibili meditates beneath an ancient carved stone tablet, seeking demon lore. He invites the characters to share his camp and trades tales of the blood demon he hunts for stories of monsters they've slain. By morning he is gone without a trace.","seed":"The mountain tower of the mage Siman is wrapped in fog and darkness. Before it fell she sent a mental call to her karkion friend Abas, who hires the characters as escort. At the tower they find a blood demon Siman summoned has broken free and now rules the tower and its people.","source":"bestiary"},
  {"kin":"Lizard People","page":28,"category":"Rare Kin","text":"Swamp and delta tribes deeply tied to water; mostly peaceful fishers, mussel farmers and traders, though some aggressive clans raid, take slaves and offer blood sacrifices.","encounter":"The characters notice lizard folk watching from roadside bushes, hissing nervously but not hostile. If the characters wait or show peaceful intent, the merchant [Click][cluck] comes out to sell smoked eel, pickled clams and fine amber jewelry, preferring metal tools or weapons as payment but accepting silver or gold.","seed":"The shaman [Shh][shh][grr][cluck] has turned twenty warriors of a once-peaceful clan into raiders who kill those who resist and seize those who surrender as sacrifices to the snake demon Sisisiss. She claims the demon speaks to her in dreams, but it's a lie to enrich herself; the characters must expose or stop her and free the captives in time.","source":"bestiary"},
  {"kin":"Satyr","page":36,"category":"Rare Kin","text":"Forest revelers who worship joy and celebrate constantly with feasting, potent satyr wine, dance and music.","encounter":"Music and laughter lead to a forest feast of satyrs, centaurs and naiads that anyone may join. It lasts all night and breaks up by dawn; joining gives a wild break from adventuring, and Performance rolls can win satyr friends, while sourpuss guests earn no respect.","seed":"A gaunt, melancholy satyr named Spiros, newly escaped from a traveling jester troupe that caged and exhibited him for years, asks for help finding his friends at the greatest feast in the forest. Cheered by the characters, he tries to turn the trip into a traveling party — but the jesters are tracking them to reclaim their 'property'.","source":"bestiary"}
];

